brigade@monger.net wrote:
>
>In summary, is the following true? (remember this is 1.4f)
>
>1. Either need a ring of fire resistance or by eating a monster that
>gives it to you before entering hell (level 40)(Is a Dragon one such
>example? any others?)

IIRC a dragon (equivalent to the red dragon found in 2.3e and later) does
give fire resistance.  Hell hounds also might, but you have to be *in*
Hell to find one; and since they're 'd' they might confer aggravate
monster (they don't in the modern game).

>2. Once down to the maze levels...you must find the a teleport trap?
>(will there always be one somewhere)? Do you need teleport control?

You do need teleport control to select the level, but a confused scroll of
teleportation works the same as in the modern game.  You may have noticed
that there's no stunning; eating a bat will confuse you.

>3. Are there really wands of wishing tucked under dead end areas
>behind boulders?  Do you need a wand of digging to get at them?  Just
>have to hope ya find one?

The code seems to place one wand of wishing in each non-Hell maze.  (This
feature was nerfed in 2.2a.) To get at it, either dig, bust the boulder
with a wand of striking or a pickaxe, or drop your gear and squeeze into
the square with the boulder.  Alas, from what I remember of playing pre-3.0
NetHacks, the only sure ways to get a pickaxe are to wish or to be an
Archeologist.

Try a potion of object detection to find possible places to look for the
wand of wishing.

>4. Any other necessities?

Telepathy and a means of blinding yourself will identify the level with the
Wizard.  If you don't have a blindfold, try bouncing a lightning bolt off a
wall; lightning does no harm to rings or wands as it does in the modern
game.  If you see a demon in the center room, pass him by; he carries a
fake Amulet.

You'll need to be able to cross water to get into the Wizard's stronghold.
Stepping into water is an instadeath unless you have teleportitis.  (I lost
so many promising characters that way, playing 2.3e.)  You'll also need
some means of digging, or of morphing into a xorn, to get into the Wizard's
stronghold.  Or you might use a wand of digging and hit the Wizard with
some ranged attacks.

The Wizard can summon nasties; a ring of conflict can make them a lot less
vexing.

